  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Morocco: Voluntary Return and Reintegration for Migrants in Vulnerable Situation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on 15 years of experience in Morocco, this project aims to contribute to improving the migration management system through migrants&apos; protection. It will reach this objective by offering the alternative of assisted voluntary return and reintegration to a maximum number of 400 migrants in vulnerable situations in Morocco. The different components of this project will have a specific focus on migrants in vulnerable situation especially unaccompanied migrant children, aged-out beneficiaries, migrants with health needs, potential victims of trafficking and those exposed to gender-related vulnerabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
